\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Polynomial weights and the discarded fluctuation}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{At fixed block field, a fine site is its lifted block value plus
an independent centered Gaussian fluctuation. A square therefore
acquires the fluctuation variance under averaging, and a fourth power
acquires terms of degrees two and zero. Can lower powers be subtracted
in advance so that a polynomial keeps its degree and changes only by
a scalar under the rescaled mean?}
